  "status_text": "One list of possible drops now works for every switch setting. Lean checked this when each answer has two regions defined by fixed switches, one requiring zero and one requiring one. If chains of drops are bounded, list the sets of distinct answers that can drop from one to zero in some order as switches turn on. At a given setting, keep the sets whose required switches are all on. The largest surviving set gives the exact longest chain below that setting, and the same list gives one filling that respects every required answer (L-lib-1241).",
